{
  "name": "summarize-notes",
  "description": "For every Markdown file in a notes directory, write a one-paragraph summary, then combine all summaries into SUMMARY.md.",
  "inputs": { "notes_dir": "string" },
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "step",
      "id": "summarize",
      "agent": "wf-coder",
      "prompt": "Goal: for every Markdown file in the notes directory, write a one-paragraph summary of that file's content.\n\nNotes directory: {{notes_dir}}\n\nDo the following:\n1. List every Markdown file (*.md) directly in {{notes_dir}}. Exclude {{notes_dir}}/SUMMARY.md itself if it already exists, so a re-run does not summarize its own output. Handle whatever Markdown files are present — do not assume any specific filenames.\n2. Read each file's content and write a single, concise one-paragraph summary of it.\n3. Collect these into one intermediate file at {{notes_dir}}/.summaries.md, with one section per source file: a heading naming the file (e.g. its filename) followed by that file's one-paragraph summary.\n\nIf {{notes_dir}} does not exist or contains no Markdown files, write {{notes_dir}}/.summaries.md stating that no notes were found, and say so in your final message.\n\nYour final message must report how many files you summarized and confirm {{notes_dir}}/.summaries.md was written.",
      "artifacts": { "summaries": "{{notes_dir}}/.summaries.md" }
    },
    {
      "type": "step",
      "id": "combine",
      "agent": "wf-coder",
      "effortLevel": "low",
      "prompt": "Goal: combine the per-file summaries into a single SUMMARY.md.\n\nRead the per-file summaries from {{artifacts.summaries}}. Compose them into a clean, well-organized Markdown document and write it to {{notes_dir}}/SUMMARY.md. Give it a top-level title, then one section per note file preserving each file's one-paragraph summary and a clear reference to which source file it came from. Do not invent content beyond what the summaries contain.\n\nIf {{artifacts.summaries}} indicates no notes were found, write {{notes_dir}}/SUMMARY.md with a title and a short note that there were no Markdown files to summarize.\n\nYour final message must confirm {{notes_dir}}/SUMMARY.md was written.",
      "artifacts": { "summary": "{{notes_dir}}/SUMMARY.md" }
    }
  ]
}
SUMMARY:
summarize-notes: summarize every Markdown file in notes/ then combine into notes/SUMMARY.md.
summarize (wf-coder): lists all *.md in {{notes_dir}} (excluding SUMMARY.md), writes a one-paragraph summary per file to {{notes_dir}}/.summaries.md.
combine (wf-coder, low effort): reads the .summaries.md artifact and composes notes/SUMMARY.md.
No loop; two sequential steps passing data via {{artifacts.summaries}}.
Reusable via the notes_dir input; no filenames hardcoded. No .kiro/agents dependencies (uses bundled wf-coder).

